{#
  HOMEPAGE. Hand-composed (no reframe/story/practical template) by design: the
  three page templates all open breadcrumbs, hero, lead, then their fixed block
  order, and the front door should not read like the twenty-third service page.
  Composed from the shared library instead, with two homepage-specific components
  added to that library rather than inlined here (s.homeHero and s.videoEmbed,
  numbered 18 and 19 in components/sections.njk).

  BRIEF FIDELITY (SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md, "/ Homepage"):
  - Title tag: exact.
  - Meta: matches the brief except "Free 15-minute call" is corrected to
    "Free 15 to 20 minute call". CLIENT_FACTS.md outranks SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md on
    facts, and the offering is a free 15 to 20 minute Get to Know Us call.
  - H1: the brief offers the brand tagline or a warmer variant. Using the tagline
    ("Navigating Life's Waves Together") since it is the brand lockup and the
    brief's first choice. The target keyword ("therapist Laguna Beach") therefore
    carries in the title tag, meta, eyebrow, hero lead, and the section h2s
    instead of the h1.
  - Every section the brief lists is present: hero with the intro copy, the
    three-tier proof rendered as warmth, the Beach Therapy teaser, the who-we-help
    grid, the what-people-struggle-with grid, the team teaser, the out-of-network
    and Superbill line, and the gold CTA band. Plus the approved pull-quote.
  - Internal links: /beach-therapy, /get-started, /about/kay-wenger,
    /about/our-team, /fees, all six /therapy/* and all nine /specialties/*.
  - Schema: WebSite + a MedicalBusiness @id reference, not a redefinition. The
    full business record lives on /contact (SCHEMA.md).

  No breadcrumbs: this is the root, and a one-item trail is noise.
  Gold discipline: two gold actions on the page (hero and CTA band), a full page
  apart, so no viewport ever shows two. Every other action is navy or teal.
  Facts come from site.json and nav.json, never hardcoded. No em dashes.
#}
