{#
  THE INTRO VIDEO. Client-supplied YouTube embed.
  Three deliberate changes to the supplied iframe, all noted back to the client:
  1. youtube.com becomes youtube-nocookie.com. Same video, but YouTube sets no
     tracking cookie until playback. On a mental-health site, where the visit
     itself is sensitive, that is the right default.
  2. The "si" share-tracking parameter is dropped.
  3. Fixed 560x315 becomes a fluid 16:9 wrapper, so it fits every breakpoint and
     reserves its own space (no layout shift).
  4. controls=0 REMOVED. It was in the supplied embed and was kept on the first
     pass, but hiding the player control bar takes away pause, volume, playback
     speed and the captions button, which is a real accessibility barrier and not
     something the surrounding copy can compensate for. Default controls restored.
  loading="lazy" keeps the whole YouTube payload off the critical path, and
  playback is click-initiated and never autoplays.
#}
{{ s.videoEmbed({
  tone: "paper",
  eyebrow: "In our own words",
  title: "Hear how we think about",
  titleEmphasis: "the work.",
  lead: "Choosing a therapist off a website is a strange thing to have to do. This one is on marriage and family therapy, which is as good a window as any into how the work actually goes here.",
  src: "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/ipWH9vtJPVk",
  title_: "Marriage and Family Therapy: Improve Your Marriage, Improve your Relationships, from Laguna Beach Counseling",
  caption: "Marriage and Family Therapy: Improve Your Marriage, Improve your Relationships."
}) }}

